<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Jan industry output falls 1.7 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Jan industry output falls 1.7 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT  Jan 97     Dec 96	Jan 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   -1.7	 +0.8	 -0.5</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +1.7	 +2.9	 -1.1</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		97.9	 99.6	 96.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics. @ The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				    Jan 97		   Dec 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining			74.8	-3.2	77.3	+2.8</p>
<p> Manufacturing output    98.6	+1.4	97.2	-0.2</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods    99.4	-2.1     101.5	+0.6</p>
<p>	Capital goods     103.2	+7.5	96.0	-1.2</p>
<p>	Consumer durables  85.7	+3.3	83.0	-2.6</p>
<p>	Consumer goods     94.5	-2.3	96.7	+0.9</p>
<p> Energy output	    108.0	+1.0     106.9	+3.4</p>
<p> Construction		92.3     -25.0     123.1	+7.2 @</p>
<p>Two month comparison Dec '96/Jan '97 with Oct/Nov 1996:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +0.5</p>
<p> Manufacturing output		  +1.0</p>
<p> Construction			    -7.0</p>
<p> Capital goods			   +4.0</p>
<p> Mining				    +1.5</p>
<p> Energy output			   +3.0</p>
<p> Consumer durables and goods	 unch</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    -0.5 @</p>
</text>
